# RAG and data

A retrieval result is not a finished RAG system. Design ingestion, parsing, chunking, metadata, embedding, filters, and context construction around the user task.

Use hybrid search or reranking only when an evaluation shows a gain. Record the embedding model and index configuration as versioned behavior.

Citations must point at sources the retriever actually returned. Measure citation precision and recall when answers depend on sources.

Evaluate with Recall@K, Precision@K, MRR, NDCG, or a justified substitute on a real dataset. A hand-picked demo is not an evaluation.

Define document update and deletion behavior before indexing production data.
